  "notes": [
    "CT-RGO-1: week 1 of the wave tops out at 85% of TM, about 76% of e1RM with TM at 90%; weeks 2 and 3 reach 81% and 86%. The optional extra triple at 80% of e1RM after week 1's AMRAP is not drafted.",
    "CT-RGO-6: Activate (or equivalent) 3 times a week counts team trainings; if the team runs fewer than 3, the hand-over says so. No day is added.",
    "CT-RGO-7, CT-RGO-8: Limber 11 opens every gym session and is labelled mobility preparation, never injury prevention. CT-RGO-11: neck work is labelled performance and robustness work, never concussion prevention.",
    "CT-RGO-4: max-velocity sprints come before lifting. On the 2-day layout they share the Limber 11 warm-up segment, and the 2- and 3-day deload weeks drop the sprints and neck work to keep each Notes cell within VO-1's 20 words; the 4-day and the 3-day sprint day keep them.",
    "CT-RGO-12: every accessory and supplemental set stops at RIR 3 or more, so no AMRAP Last Set rows (A-3 gives way under G-20).",
    "L-17: squat is high bar for club lifters; the name stays Squat (LB-6).",
    "In-season (CT-RGI) rules are not in this template, so an in-season block can't be drafted from it."
  ]
